<div class="shell hero-inner"><div><div class="eyebrow">Expedition Growth Lab</div><h1>Protect the Build.<br><em>Grow the Legacy.</em></h1><p class="hero-copy">XGL helps founder-led builders, manufacturers, fabricators, expedition companies, and outdoor businesses become stronger without becoming less themselves. We work on the systems around the craft: growth, operations, relationships, intelligence, and the machinery that lets a good company keep being good as it grows.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/the-lab">Enter the Lab</a><a class="button secondary" href="/command-central">Open Command Central</a></div></div><aside class="hero-note"><strong>Built for people who make, move, repair, sell, and stand behind real things.</strong><p>Human-scale growth. Better systems. Clearer decisions. No sanding off the culture to make the spreadsheet prettier.</p></aside></div></header>
<main>
<section class="section alt"><div class="shell grid2"><div><div class="kicker">What XGL is</div><h2 class="section-title">A growth partner with grease under its fingernails.</h2></div><div><p class="lede">Growth should not cost you the thing worth growing.</p><div class="bodycopy"><p>XGL sits somewhere between a consultancy, intelligence desk, business helpdesk, systems shop, and long-term field partner.</p><p>We look at the whole build: customers, sales, operations, people, technology, risk, reputation, industry terrain, and the founder carrying too much of it personally.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="kicker">The operating map</div><h2 class="section-title">Four ways into XGL.</h2><div class="grid4" style="margin-top:58px"><article class="pillar"><span class="num">01</span><h3>The Lab</h3><p>Diagnose the business, build stronger systems, remove drag, and give the founder room to lead.</p></article><article class="pillar"><span class="num">02</span><h3>Command Central</h3><p>Live industry intelligence: events, deadlines, regulation, public lands, builder signals, and field context.</p></article><article class="pillar"><span class="num">03</span><h3>One Rising Sun</h3><p>A selective partnership ecosystem connecting independent capability without turning it into consolidation.</p></article><article class="pillar"><span class="num">04</span><h3>Field Partnership</h3><p>Hands-on problem solving for companies whose growth is outrunning the systems underneath it.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section light"><div class="shell grid2"><div><div class="kicker">How we think</div><h2 class="section-title">Good companies deserve better than generic business advice.</h2></div><div class="path-list"><div class="path"><span>01</span><strong>Protect what already works.</strong><em>Preserve craft</em></div><div class="path"><span>02</span><strong>Fix the machinery around the work.</strong><em>Build systems</em></div><div class="path"><span>03</span><strong>Give founders better information.</strong><em>Improve judgment</em></div><div class="path"><span>04</span><strong>Grow without surrendering independence.</strong><em>Keep control</em></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section alt"><div class="shell grid2"><div class="quote"><p>“For nearly twenty years, I worked on the systems behind the walls. Now I work on the systems behind the builders.”</p><small>Brian Reymore · Expedition Growth Lab</small></div><div><div class="kicker">Why this exists</div><h2 class="section-title">Built from the work, not from a pitch deck.</h2><div class="bodycopy"><p>XGL comes from years of repair, fabrication, logistics, transportation, warehousing, sales, management, customer service, and entrepreneurship.</p><p>That history matters because the companies we serve do not live in abstract strategy slides. They live in shops, trucks, warehouses, booths, job sites, trailheads, inboxes, warranty queues, and Monday mornings.</p></div><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/about">Why XGL exists</a></div></div></div></section>
<section class="cta"><div class="shell"><div class="kicker" style="justify-content:center">Start where the friction is</div><h2>Let’s talk about your build.</h2><p>You do not need to arrive with a perfect brief. Bring the problem, the bottleneck, the opportunity, or the thing that keeps waking you up at 3 a.m.</p><div class="actions" style="justify-content:center"><a class="button primary" href="/contact">Start a Conversation</a><a class="button secondary" href="/the-lab">See how the Lab works</a></div></div></section>
